---
description: Atlas OS visual and interaction principles
globs: src/**/*.{css,tsx,ts}
alwaysApply: false
---

Design for a cinematic private command environment, not a SaaS dashboard.

Palette: true obsidian, deep luxury gold, deep luxury purple. No neon, no cheap gradients, no gamer glow, no stock card grids.

Atlas should feel present. Navigation supports intelligence; it does not dominate it.

Use layout modes (`compact` / `command` / `expanded`) so fold-closed, fold-open, and desktop can become distinct experiences.

Motion: transform and opacity only, purposeful, interruptible, reduced-motion safe. No Three.js or decorative WebGL.

Do not use shadcn or default Tailwind component aesthetics. Tokens and CSS own the look.

Empty states are honest. Do not populate the shell with placeholder intelligence.
